# A line break after a colon indents two spaces, and the next keeps that
# indent. Shift+Tab takes two spaces off the line the cursor is on, and the
# cursor goes with the text it was after: column 4 on "  y" becomes 2 on "y".
# frames 10
# expect text def f:\n  x = 1\ny
# expect cursor 3 2
1 text def f:
2 key enter
3 text x = 1
4 key enter
5 text y
6 key tab shift
